# Intestate Succession Act 1967

## Section 1 — Short title

## Section 2 — Application

<!-- l4: decide:section 2 — nothing in this Act applies to the estate -->

**1.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 2 — nothing in this Act applies to the estate means the deceased person's a Muslim.

<!-- l4: decide:this Act applies to the estate -->

**2.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, this Act applies to the estate if it is not the case that section 2 — nothing in this Act applies to the estate with the deceased person.

## Section 3 — Interpretation

<!-- l4: decide:section 3 — a “child” within the meaning of this Act -->

**3.** In relation to a Child “the relationship of child to parent”, section 3 — a “child” within the meaning of this Act if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) means a legitimate child; and

        (ii) the relationship of child to parent's a legitimate child of the person whose child he is; or

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) and includes any child adopted by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam; and

        (ii) the relationship of child to parent's adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam.

<!-- l4: decide:the will beneficially disposes of the whole of his property -->

**4.** In relation to a Will “the will”, the will beneficially disposes of the whole of his property means any with a universal or residuary beneficial gift and the will's the dispositions made by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:a universal or residuary beneficial gift -->

**5.** In relation to a Disposition “the disposition”, a universal or residuary beneficial gift if—

    (a) the disposition's beneficial; and

    (b) consider the case distinctions of the disposition's the kind of disposition :  when a universal gift has  then TRUE. when a residuary gift has  then TRUE. when a specific devise or bequest has  then FALSE. when a pecuniary legacy has  then FALSE. when an appointment by will under a power has  then FALSE. when a charge or direction for the payment of a debt has  then FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:section 3 — an “intestate” within the meaning of this Act -->

**6.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 3 — an “intestate” within the meaning of this Act means consider the case distinctions of the deceased person's the will :  when NOTHING has  then TRUE. when JUST has a will then not the will beneficially disposes of the whole of his property with a will.

## Section 4 — Law regulating distribution

<!-- l4: decide:section 4(1) — the law of the country of domicile is the law of Singapore -->

**7.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 4(1) — the law of the country of domicile is the law of Singapore means the deceased person's domiciled in Singapore at the time of his death.

<!-- l4: decide:section 4(2) — the distribution of the immovable property is regulated by this Act -->

**8.** Section 4(2) — the distribution of the immovable property is regulated by this Act means TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:section 4 — the value of the property whose distribution is regulated by this Act -->

**9.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 4 — the value of the property whose distribution is regulated by this Act means the sum of if section 4(1) — the law of the country of domicile is the law of Singapore with the deceased person then the sum of the estate's the value of the movable property situated in Singapore and the estate's the value of the movable property situated outside Singapore else 0 and if section 4(2) — the distribution of the immovable property is regulated by this Act then the sum of the estate's the value of the immovable property situated in Singapore and the estate's the value of the immovable property situated outside Singapore else 0.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the estate” means the deceased person's the estate;

## Section 5 — Property of intestate to be distributed

<!-- l4: decide:2 June 1967 -->

**10.** 2 June 1967 means YMD with 1967, 6 and 2.

<!-- l4: decide:the date of the death of the intestate -->

**11.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the date of the death of the intestate means consider the case distinctions of the deceased person's the deceased's vital status :  when living has  then NOTHING. when died on has the date of death then JUST with the date of death. when dead, the date of death not known has  then NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:section 5 — the person dies intestate after 2 June 1967 -->

**12.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 5 — the person dies intestate after 2 June 1967 if—

    (a) section 3 — an “intestate” within the meaning of this Act with the deceased person; and

    (b) consider the case distinctions of the date of the death of the intestate with the deceased person :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has the date of death then Day with the date of death is greater than Day with 2 June 1967.

<!-- l4: decide:section 5(a) — domiciled in Singapore and possessed beneficially of property situated in Singapore -->

**13.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 5(a) — domiciled in Singapore and possessed beneficially of property situated in Singapore if—

    (a) domiciled in Singapore;

    (b) the deceased person's domiciled in Singapore at the time of his death;

    (c) and possessed beneficially of property, whether movable or immovable, or both, situated in Singapore; and

    (d) the property situated in Singapore, whether movable or immovable, or both, possessed beneficially with the deceased person is greater than 0.

<!-- l4: decide:section 5(b) — domiciled outside Singapore and possessed beneficially of immovable property situated in Singapore -->

**14.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 5(b) — domiciled outside Singapore and possessed beneficially of immovable property situated in Singapore if—

    (a) domiciled outside Singapore;

    (b) it is not the case that the deceased person's domiciled in Singapore at the time of his death;

    (c) and possessed beneficially of immovable property situated in Singapore; and

    (d) the immovable property situated in Singapore, possessed beneficially with the deceased person is greater than 0.

<!-- l4: decide:the property situated in Singapore, whether movable or immovable, or both, possessed beneficially -->

**15.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the property situated in Singapore, whether movable or immovable, or both, possessed beneficially means max with 0 and the difference between the property held as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore with the deceased person and the sum of the deceased person's the estate's the value of the movable property situated in Singapore and the deceased person's the estate's the value of the immovable property situated in Singapore.

<!-- l4: decide:the immovable property situated in Singapore, possessed beneficially -->

**16.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the immovable property situated in Singapore, possessed beneficially means max with 0 and the difference between the property held as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore with the deceased person and the deceased person's the estate's the value of the immovable property situated in Singapore.

<!-- l4: decide:the property held as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore -->

**17.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the property held as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore means the deceased person's the estate's the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore.

<!-- l4: decide:section 5 — that property -->

**18.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 5 — that property means if section 5(a) — domiciled in Singapore and possessed beneficially of property situated in Singapore with the deceased person then the property situated in Singapore, whether movable or immovable, or both, possessed beneficially with the deceased person if section 5(b) — domiciled outside Singapore and possessed beneficially of immovable property situated in Singapore with the deceased person then the immovable property situated in Singapore, possessed beneficially with the deceased person otherwise 0.

<!-- l4: decide:section 5 — the property to be distributed, after payment thereout of the expenses of due administration -->

**19.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 5 — the property to be distributed, after payment thereout of the expenses of due administration means max with 0 and the difference between the deceased person's the estate's the funeral, testamentary and administration expenses and section 5 — that property with the deceased person.

## Section 6 — Persons held to be similarly related to deceased

<!-- l4: decide:section 6(a) — there shall be no distinction between those related through his father and those related through his mother -->

**20.** Section 6(a) — there shall be no distinction between those related through his father and those related through his mother means TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:actually born in the lifetime of the intestate -->

**21.** In relation to a Person “the person” and an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate”, actually born in the lifetime of the intestate means consider the case distinctions of the person's date of birth :  when NOTHING has  then TRUE. when JUST has the date of birth then consider the case distinctions of the date of the death of the intestate :  when NOTHING has  then TRUE. when JUST has the day the intestate died then Day with the date of birth is at most Day with the day the intestate died.

<!-- l4: decide:section 6(a) — actually born in his lifetime, or at the date of his death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive -->

**22.** In relation to a Person “the person” and an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate”, section 6(a) — actually born in his lifetime, or at the date of his death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) those who were actually born in his lifetime; and

        (ii) actually born in the lifetime of the intestate with the person and the date of the death of the intestate; or

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) those who at the date of his death were only conceived in the womb but who have subsequently been born alive; and

        (ii) the person's at the date of the death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive.

<!-- l4: decide:related to the deceased by the whole blood -->

**23.** In relation to a Collateral relative “the relative”, related to the deceased by the whole blood means consider the case distinctions of the relative's of the whole blood or of the half blood :  when of the whole blood has  then TRUE. when of the half blood has  then FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:related to the deceased by the half blood -->

**24.** In relation to a Collateral relative “the relative”, related to the deceased by the half blood if it is not the case that related to the deceased by the whole blood with the relative.

<!-- l4: decide:section 6(b) — those of the whole blood, the half blood ranking immediately after them -->

**25.** In relation to a list of Collateral relative “the relatives of one degree”, section 6(b) — those of the whole blood, the half blood ranking immediately after them means if null with those of the whole blood, then those of the half blood; otherwise, those of the whole blood.

For the purposes of this provision—

“those of the whole blood” means filter with related to the deceased by the whole blood and the relatives of one degree;

“those of the half blood” means filter with related to the deceased by the half blood and the relatives of one degree;

## Section 7 — Rules for distribution — the facts the nine rules read

<!-- l4: decide:the person survives the intestate -->

**26.** In relation to a Person “the person” and an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate”, the person survives the intestate means consider the case distinctions of the person's vital status :  when living has  then TRUE. when died on has the date of death then consider the case distinctions of the date of the death of the intestate :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has the day the intestate died then Day with the date of death is greater than Day with the day the intestate died. when dead, the date of death not known has  then FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the person survives the intestate and is within the classes section 6(a) names -->

**27.** In relation to a Person “the person” and an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate”, the person survives the intestate and is within the classes section 6(a) names if—

    (a) the person survives the intestate with the person and the date of the death of the intestate; and

    (b) section 6(a) — actually born in his lifetime, or at the date of his death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive with the person and the date of the death of the intestate.

<!-- l4: decide:the spouses surviving the intestate -->

**28.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the spouses surviving the intestate means filter with a subsisting marriage to a spouse who survives the intestate and the deceased person's the family's the marriages of the deceased.

For the purposes of this provision—

“a subsisting marriage to a spouse who survives the intestate” means the marriage's subsisting at the death of the deceased, in the sense of not dissolved or annulled before the death and the person survives the intestate and is within the classes section 6(a) names with the marriage's the spouse and the date of the death of the intestate with the deceased person;

<!-- l4: decide:the intestate leaves a surviving spouse -->

**29.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the intestate leaves a surviving spouse if it is not the case that null with the spouses surviving the intestate with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:the parents of the intestate who survive him -->

**30.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the parents of the intestate who survive him means filter with a parent who survives the intestate and append with maybeToList with the deceased person's the family's the father of the deceased and maybeToList with the deceased person's the family's the mother of the deceased.

For the purposes of this provision—

“a parent who survives the intestate” means the person survives the intestate and is within the classes section 6(a) names with the parent and the date of the death of the intestate with the deceased person;

<!-- l4: decide:the grandparents of the intestate who survive him -->

**31.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the grandparents of the intestate who survive him means filter with a grandparent who survives the intestate and the deceased person's the family's the grandparents of the deceased.

For the purposes of this provision—

“a grandparent who survives the intestate” means the person survives the intestate and is within the classes section 6(a) names with the grandparent and the date of the death of the intestate with the deceased person;

<!-- l4: decide:the uncles and aunts of the intestate who survive him -->

**32.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the uncles and aunts of the intestate who survive him means filter with an uncle or aunt who survives the intestate and the deceased person's the family's the uncles and aunts of the deceased.

For the purposes of this provision—

“an uncle or aunt who survives the intestate” means the person survives the intestate and is within the classes section 6(a) names with the relative's the relative and the date of the death of the intestate with the deceased person;

<!-- l4: decide:the entitlement of -->

**33.** In relation to a Person “the person” and a Share “the fraction of the property distributable under this Act”, the entitlement of means Entitlement where the person entitled is an individual with the person and the fraction of the property distributable under this Act is the fraction of the property distributable under this Act.

## Section 7 rule 3 — per stirpes, and the two provisos

<!-- l4: decide:rule 3 — this child is a stock which takes, in his own right or through those who legally represent him -->

**34.** In relation to a Child “the relationship of child to parent” and an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate”, rule 3 — this child is a stock which takes, in his own right or through those who legally represent him if—

    (a) section 3 — a “child” within the meaning of this Act with the relationship of child to parent;

    (b) section 6(a) — actually born in his lifetime, or at the date of his death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive with the relationship of child to parent's the child and the date of the death of the intestate; and

    (c) any of the following applies—

        (i) the person survives the intestate with the relationship of child to parent's the child and the date of the death of the intestate; or

        (ii) rule 3 — the ancestor leaves a child who takes, or who is himself represented with the relationship of child to parent's the child and the date of the death of the intestate.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 3 — the ancestor leaves a child who takes, or who is himself represented -->

**35.** In relation to a Person “the ancestor” and an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate”, rule 3 — the ancestor leaves a child who takes, or who is himself represented means any with a stock of this ancestor which takes and the ancestor's children.

For the purposes of this provision—

“a stock of this ancestor which takes” means rule 3 — this child is a stock which takes, in his own right or through those who legally represent him with the relationship of child to parent and the date of the death of the intestate;

<!-- l4: decide:rule 3 — divided by equal portions per stirpes -->

**36.** In relation to a Person “the ancestor”, an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate” and a Share “the share to be divided”, rule 3 — divided by equal portions per stirpes means if count with the stocks is equal to 0, then EMPTY; otherwise, concat with map with the takers of one stock and the stocks.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the stocks” means filter with a stock of this ancestor which takes and the ancestor's children;

“a stock of this ancestor which takes” means rule 3 — this child is a stock which takes, in his own right or through those who legally represent him with the relationship of child to parent and the date of the death of the intestate;

“the share of one stock” means the result of dividing the share to be divided by count with the stocks;

“the takers of one stock” means if the person survives the intestate and is within the classes section 6(a) names with the relationship of child to parent's the child and the date of the death of the intestate, then list of the entitlement of with the relationship of child to parent's the child and the share of one stock; otherwise, rule 3 — divided by equal portions per stirpes with the relationship of child to parent's the child, the date of the death of the intestate and the share of one stock;

<!-- l4: decide:the intestate leaves issue -->

**37.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the intestate leaves issue means rule 3 — the ancestor leaves a child who takes, or who is himself represented with the deceased person's the deceased and the date of the death of the intestate with the deceased person.

## Section 7 rules 1, 2 and 4 — the surviving spouse

<!-- l4: decide:rule 1 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse, no issue and no parent -->

**38.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 1 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse, no issue and no parent if—

    (a) leaving a surviving spouse;

    (b) the intestate leaves a surviving spouse with the deceased person;

    (c) no issue;

    (d) it is not the case that the intestate leaves issue with the deceased person;

    (e) and no parent; and

    (f) null with the parents of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 2 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse and issue -->

**39.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 2 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse and issue if—

    (a) leaving a surviving spouse;

    (b) the intestate leaves a surviving spouse with the deceased person;

    (c) and issue; and

    (d) the intestate leaves issue with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 4 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse and no issue but a parent or parents -->

**40.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 4 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse and no issue but a parent or parents if—

    (a) leaving a surviving spouse;

    (b) the intestate leaves a surviving spouse with the deceased person;

    (c) and no issue;

    (d) it is not the case that the intestate leaves issue with the deceased person;

    (e) but a parent or parents; and

    (f) it is not the case that null with the parents of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:the share of the estate to which the surviving spouse is entitled -->

**41.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the share of the estate to which the surviving spouse is entitled means if rule 1 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse, no issue and no parent with the deceased person then 1 if rule 2 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse and issue with the deceased person then the result of dividing 1 by 2 if rule 4 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse and no issue but a parent or parents with the deceased person then the result of dividing 1 by 2 otherwise 0.

## Section 7 rule 3 — the share the issue take

<!-- l4: decide:rule 3 — the share of the estate distributed among the issue, subject to the rights of the surviving spouse -->

**42.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 3 — the share of the estate distributed among the issue, subject to the rights of the surviving spouse means if the intestate leaves issue with the deceased person, then the difference between the share of the estate to which the surviving spouse is entitled with the deceased person and 1; otherwise, 0.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 3 — the entitlements of the issue -->

**43.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 3 — the entitlements of the issue means rule 3 — divided by equal portions per stirpes with the deceased person's the deceased, the date of the death of the intestate with the deceased person and rule 3 — the share of the estate distributed among the issue, subject to the rights of the surviving spouse with the deceased person.

## Section 7 rules 4 and 5 — the parents

<!-- l4: decide:rule 4 — the share of the estate to which the parent or parents are entitled -->

**44.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 4 — the share of the estate to which the parent or parents are entitled means if rule 4 — an intestate dies leaving a surviving spouse and no issue but a parent or parents with the deceased person, then the result of dividing 1 by 2; otherwise, 0.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 5 — the share of the estate the parent or parents take -->

**45.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 5 — the share of the estate the parent or parents take means if rule 5 — there are no descendants, and there are a parent or parents of the intestate with the deceased person, then the difference between the share of the estate to which the surviving spouse is entitled with the deceased person and 1; otherwise, 0.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 5 — there are no descendants, and there are a parent or parents of the intestate -->

**46.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 5 — there are no descendants, and there are a parent or parents of the intestate if—

    (a) If there are no descendants;

    (b) there are not descendants with the deceased person;

    (c) the parent or parents of the intestate; and

    (d) it is not the case that null with the parents of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 5 — the entitlements of the parent or parents -->

**47.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 5 — the entitlements of the parent or parents means if not rule 5 — there are no descendants, and there are a parent or parents of the intestate with the deceased person, then EMPTY; otherwise, map with the entitlement of one parent and the parents.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the parents” means the parents of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person;

“the entitlement of one parent” means the entitlement of with the parent and the result of dividing rule 5 — the share of the estate the parent or parents take with the deceased person by count with the parents;

## Section 7 rule 6 — brothers and sisters, and the children of deceased brothers or sisters

<!-- l4: decide:rule 6 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants or parents -->

**48.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 6 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants or parents if—

    (a) no surviving spouse;

    (b) it is not the case that the intestate leaves a surviving spouse with the deceased person;

    (c) descendants;

    (d) there are not descendants with the deceased person;

    (e) or parents; and

    (f) null with the parents of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 6 — the children of a deceased brother or sister who take according to their stocks -->

**49.** In relation to a Collateral relative “the brother or sister” and an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate”, rule 6 — the children of a deceased brother or sister who take according to their stocks means map with the person who is that child and filter with a child of the brother or sister who takes and the brother or sister's the relative's children.

For the purposes of this provision—

“a child of the brother or sister who takes” means section 3 — a “child” within the meaning of this Act with the relationship of child to parent and section 6(a) — actually born in his lifetime, or at the date of his death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive with the relationship of child to parent's the child and the date of the death of the intestate and the person survives the intestate with the relationship of child to parent's the child and the date of the death of the intestate;

“the person who is that child” means the relationship of child to parent's the child;

<!-- l4: decide:rule 6 — this brother or sister shares, or has children who take according to their stocks -->

**50.** In relation to a Collateral relative “the brother or sister” and an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate”, rule 6 — this brother or sister shares, or has children who take according to their stocks if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) the brothers and sisters ... shall share the estate in equal portions between the brothers and sisters; and

        (ii) the person survives the intestate and is within the classes section 6(a) names with the brother or sister's the relative and the date of the death of the intestate; or

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) and the children of any deceased brother or sister shall take according to their stocks;

        (ii) it is not the case that the person survives the intestate with the brother or sister's the relative and the date of the death of the intestate; and

        (iii) it is not the case that null with rule 6 — the children of a deceased brother or sister who take according to their stocks with the brother or sister and the date of the death of the intestate.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 6 — the stocks of brothers and sisters between which the estate is shared in equal portions -->

**51.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 6 — the stocks of brothers and sisters between which the estate is shared in equal portions means section 6(b) — those of the whole blood, the half blood ranking immediately after them with filter with a brother or sister whose stock takes and the deceased person's the family's the brothers and sisters of the deceased.

For the purposes of this provision—

“a brother or sister whose stock takes” means rule 6 — this brother or sister shares, or has children who take according to their stocks with the brother or sister and the date of the death of the intestate with the deceased person;

<!-- l4: decide:rule 6 — the takers of the share which the brother or sister would have taken -->

**52.** In relation to a Collateral relative “the brother or sister”, an optional DATE “the date of the death of the intestate” and a Share “the share of one stock”, rule 6 — the takers of the share which the brother or sister would have taken means if the person survives the intestate and is within the classes section 6(a) names with the brother or sister's the relative and the date of the death of the intestate, then list of the entitlement of with the brother or sister's the relative and the share of one stock; otherwise, map with the entitlement of one child of the deceased brother or sister and the children who take.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the children who take” means rule 6 — the children of a deceased brother or sister who take according to their stocks with the brother or sister and the date of the death of the intestate;

“the entitlement of one child of the deceased brother or sister” means the entitlement of with the child and the result of dividing the share of one stock by count with the children who take;

<!-- l4: decide:rule 6 — the entitlements of the brothers and sisters and the children of deceased brothers or sisters -->

**53.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 6 — the entitlements of the brothers and sisters and the children of deceased brothers or sisters means if not rule 6 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants or parents with the deceased person or count with the stocks is equal to 0, then EMPTY; otherwise, concat with map with the takers of one stock and the stocks.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the stocks” means rule 6 — the stocks of brothers and sisters between which the estate is shared in equal portions with the deceased person;

“the takers of one stock” means rule 6 — the takers of the share which the brother or sister would have taken with the brother or sister, the date of the death of the intestate with the deceased person and the result of dividing 1 by count with the stocks;

## Section 7 rule 7 — the grandparents

<!-- l4: decide:rule 7 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants, parents, brothers and sisters or children of such brothers and sisters but grandparents of the intestate -->

**54.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 7 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants, parents, brothers and sisters or children of such brothers and sisters but grandparents of the intestate if—

    (a) no surviving spouse, descendants, parents;

    (b) rule 6 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants or parents with the deceased person;

    (c) brothers and sisters or children of such brothers and sisters;

    (d) null with rule 6 — the stocks of brothers and sisters between which the estate is shared in equal portions with the deceased person;

    (e) but grandparents of the intestate; and

    (f) it is not the case that null with the grandparents of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 7 — the entitlements of the grandparents -->

**55.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 7 — the entitlements of the grandparents means if not rule 7 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants, parents, brothers and sisters or children of such brothers and sisters but grandparents of the intestate with the deceased person, then EMPTY; otherwise, map with the entitlement of one grandparent and the grandparents.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the grandparents” means the grandparents of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person;

“the entitlement of one grandparent” means the entitlement of with the grandparent and the result of dividing 1 by count with the grandparents;

## Section 7 rule 8 — the uncles and aunts

<!-- l4: decide:rule 8 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants, parents, brothers and sisters or their children or grandparents but uncles and aunts of the intestate -->

**56.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 8 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants, parents, brothers and sisters or their children or grandparents but uncles and aunts of the intestate if—

    (a) no surviving spouse, descendants, parents;

    (b) rule 6 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants or parents with the deceased person;

    (c) brothers and sisters or their children;

    (d) null with rule 6 — the stocks of brothers and sisters between which the estate is shared in equal portions with the deceased person;

    (e) or grandparents;

    (f) null with the grandparents of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person;

    (g) but uncles and aunts of the intestate; and

    (h) it is not the case that null with the uncles and aunts of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 8 — the entitlements of the uncles and aunts -->

**57.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 8 — the entitlements of the uncles and aunts means if not rule 8 — there are no surviving spouse, descendants, parents, brothers and sisters or their children or grandparents but uncles and aunts of the intestate with the deceased person, then EMPTY; otherwise, map with the entitlement of one uncle or aunt and the uncles and aunts who take.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the uncles and aunts who take” means section 6(b) — those of the whole blood, the half blood ranking immediately after them with the uncles and aunts of the intestate who survive him with the deceased person;

“the entitlement of one uncle or aunt” means the entitlement of with the relative's the relative and the result of dividing 1 by count with the uncles and aunts who take;

## Section 8 — Special provision if intestate leaves lawful widows

<!-- l4: decide:section 8 — the intestate leaves surviving him more than one wife -->

**58.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 8 — the intestate leaves surviving him more than one wife means count with the spouses surviving the intestate with the deceased person is greater than 1.

<!-- l4: decide:section 8 — the entitlements of the surviving spouse or spouses -->

**59.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 8 — the entitlements of the surviving spouse or spouses means if null with the wives, then EMPTY; otherwise, map with the entitlement of one wife and the wives.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the wives” means the spouses surviving the intestate with the deceased person;

“the share of a sole wife” means the share of the estate to which the surviving spouse is entitled with the deceased person;

“the entitlement of one wife” means the entitlement of with the marriage's the spouse and if section 8 — the intestate leaves surviving him more than one wife with the deceased person then the result of dividing the share of a sole wife by count with the wives else the share of a sole wife;

## Section 7 rule 9 — the Government

<!-- l4: decide:rule 9 — in default of distribution under rules 1 to 8 -->

**60.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 9 — in default of distribution under rules 1 to 8 if—

    (a) this Act has effect in respect of the estate with the deceased person; and

    (b) null with the distribution under rules 1 to 8 with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:rule 9 — the entitlement of the Government -->

**61.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, rule 9 — the entitlement of the Government means if rule 9 — in default of distribution under rules 1 to 8 with the deceased person, then list of Entitlement where the person entitled is the Government and the fraction of the property distributable under this Act is 1; otherwise, EMPTY.

## Section 9 — Children’s advancement not to be taken into account

<!-- l4: decide:section 9 — the distributive share is claimed by a child or any descendant of a child of that person -->

**62.** In relation to a Person “the intestate” and a Person “the claimant”, section 9 — the distributive share is claimed by a child or any descendant of a child of that person means any with this child is the claimant, or the claimant descends from him and the intestate's children.

For the purposes of this provision—

“this child is the claimant, or the claimant descends from him” means section 3 — a “child” within the meaning of this Act with the relationship of child to parent and the relationship of child to parent's the child's the reference for this person is equal to the claimant's the reference for this person or section 9 — the distributive share is claimed by a child or any descendant of a child of that person with the relationship of child to parent's the child and the claimant;

<!-- l4: decide:section 9 — the money or other property to be taken into account in estimating such distributive share -->

**63.** In relation to a Person “the intestate” and a Person “the claimant”, section 9 — the money or other property to be taken into account in estimating such distributive share means if section 9 — the distributive share is claimed by a child or any descendant of a child of that person with the intestate and the claimant, then JUST with 0; otherwise, NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:section 9 — the distributive share of a child or a descendant of a child, estimated -->

**64.** In relation to a Person “the intestate”, a Person “the claimant”, a Share “the fraction of the property distributable under this Act” and a Money “the property of which the share is a fraction”, section 9 — the distributive share of a child or a descendant of a child, estimated means consider the case distinctions of section 9 — the money or other property to be taken into account in estimating such distributive share with the intestate and the claimant :  when NOTHING has  then NOTHING. when JUST has the advancement then JUST with the difference between the advancement and the product of the fraction of the property distributable under this Act and the property of which the share is a fraction.

## Section 10 — Application to cases of partial intestacy

<!-- l4: decide:the will makes some beneficial disposition -->

**65.** In relation to a Will “the will”, the will makes some beneficial disposition means any with a beneficial disposition and the will's the dispositions made by the will.

For the purposes of this provision—

“a beneficial disposition” means the disposition's beneficial;

<!-- l4: decide:section 10 — the person dies leaving a will beneficially disposing of part of his property -->

**66.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 10 — the person dies leaving a will beneficially disposing of part of his property means consider the case distinctions of the deceased person's the will :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has a will then the will makes some beneficial disposition with a will and not the will beneficially disposes of the whole of his property with a will.

<!-- l4: decide:section 10 — the value of the part of his property so disposed of -->

**67.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 10 — the value of the part of his property so disposed of means consider the case distinctions of the deceased person's the will :  when NOTHING has  then 0. when JUST has a will then sum with map with the value of a beneficial disposition and filter with a beneficial disposition and a will's the dispositions made by the will.

For the purposes of this provision—

“a beneficial disposition” means the disposition's beneficial;

“the value of a beneficial disposition” means the disposition's the value of the disposition;

<!-- l4: decide:the value beneficially disposed of by the will recorded in the estate agrees with the dispositions made by the will -->

**68.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the value beneficially disposed of by the will recorded in the estate agrees with the dispositions made by the will means the deceased person's the estate's the value of the property beneficially disposed of by the will is equal to section 10 — the value of the part of his property so disposed of with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:section 10 — the part of his property not so disposed of -->

**69.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 10 — the part of his property not so disposed of means if section 10 — the person dies leaving a will beneficially disposing of part of his property with the deceased person, then max with 0 and the difference between section 10 — the value of the part of his property so disposed of with the deceased person and section 5 — the property to be distributed, after payment thereout of the expenses of due administration with the deceased person; otherwise, section 5 — the property to be distributed, after payment thereout of the expenses of due administration with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:it appears by the will that the personal representative is entitled to take that part beneficially -->

**70.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, it appears by the will that the personal representative is entitled to take that part beneficially means consider the case distinctions of the deceased person's the will :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has a will then a will's it appears by the will that the personal representative is entitled to take that part beneficially.

<!-- l4: decide:section 10 proviso — the personal representative is a trustee for the persons entitled under this Act in respect of the part of the estate not expressly disposed of -->

**71.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, section 10 proviso — the personal representative is a trustee for the persons entitled under this Act in respect of the part of the estate not expressly disposed of if—

    (a) Provided that the personal representative shall ... be a trustee for the persons entitled under this Act in respect of the part of the estate not expressly disposed of;

    (b) section 10 — the person dies leaving a will beneficially disposing of part of his property with the deceased person;

    (c) unless it appears by the will that the personal representative is entitled to take that part beneficially; and

    (d) it appears by the will that the personal representative is not entitled to take that part beneficially with the deceased person.

## The Act as a whole — the gate, the fund, and the distribution

<!-- l4: decide:this Act has effect in respect of the estate -->

**72.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, this Act has effect in respect of the estate if—

    (a) this Act applies to the estate with the deceased person;

    (b) section 5 — the person dies intestate after 2 June 1967 with the deceased person; and

    (c) any of the following applies—

        (i) section 5(a) — domiciled in Singapore and possessed beneficially of property situated in Singapore with the deceased person; or

        (ii) section 5(b) — domiciled outside Singapore and possessed beneficially of immovable property situated in Singapore with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:the property of which every share under section 7 is a fraction -->

**73.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the property of which every share under section 7 is a fraction means if this Act has effect in respect of the estate with the deceased person, then section 10 — the part of his property not so disposed of with the deceased person; otherwise, 0.

<!-- l4: decide:the distribution under rules 1 to 8 -->

**74.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the distribution under rules 1 to 8 means if not this Act has effect in respect of the estate with the deceased person, then EMPTY; otherwise, concat with list of section 8 — the entitlements of the surviving spouse or spouses with the deceased person, rule 3 — the entitlements of the issue with the deceased person, rule 5 — the entitlements of the parent or parents with the deceased person, rule 6 — the entitlements of the brothers and sisters and the children of deceased brothers or sisters with the deceased person, rule 7 — the entitlements of the grandparents with the deceased person and rule 8 — the entitlements of the uncles and aunts with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:the persons entitled to succeed beneficially, and their shares -->

**75.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the persons entitled to succeed beneficially, and their shares means append with the distribution under rules 1 to 8 with the deceased person and rule 9 — the entitlement of the Government with the deceased person.

## Reading the answer

<!-- l4: decide:the name of the person entitled -->

**76.** In relation to a Person or corporation “the person entitled”, the name of the person entitled means consider the case distinctions of the person entitled :  when an individual has the individual then the individual's name. when the Public Trustee has  then the Public Trustee. when a corporation licensed as a trust company under the Trust Companies Act 2005 has the name of the corporation then the name of the corporation. when the Government has  then the Government.

<!-- l4: decide:who takes what -->

**77.** In relation to an Entitlement “the entitlement”, who takes what means concatenate the name of the person entitled with the entitlement's the person entitled,  takes  and TOSTRING with the entitlement's the fraction of the property distributable under this Act.

<!-- l4: decide:the distribution, read out -->

**78.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the distribution, read out means map with who takes what and the persons entitled to succeed beneficially, and their shares with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:the total of the shares distributed -->

**79.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the total of the shares distributed means sum with map with the fraction taken and the persons entitled to succeed beneficially, and their shares with the deceased person.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the fraction taken” means the entitlement's the fraction of the property distributable under this Act;

## Joins with the other three Acts

<!-- l4: decide:the reference for the person entitled -->

**80.** In relation to a Person or corporation “the person entitled”, the reference for the person entitled means consider the case distinctions of the person entitled :  when an individual has the individual then JUST with the individual's the reference for this person. when the Public Trustee has  then NOTHING. when a corporation licensed as a trust company under the Trust Companies Act 2005 has the name of the corporation then NOTHING. when the Government has  then NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:the entitlements under this Act taken by an infant concerned in the estate -->

**81.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the entitlements under this Act taken by an infant concerned in the estate means filter with taken by an infant concerned in the estate and the persons entitled to succeed beneficially, and their shares with the deceased person.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the references of the infants concerned in the estate” means map with given the infant then the infant's the infant's the reference for this person and the deceased person's the infants concerned in the estate;

“taken by an infant concerned in the estate” means consider the case distinctions of the reference for the person entitled with the entitlement's the person entitled :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has the reference then elem with the reference and the references of the infants concerned in the estate;

<!-- l4: decide:the shares taken by an infant concerned in the estate, read out -->

**82.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the shares taken by an infant concerned in the estate, read out means map with who takes what and the entitlements under this Act taken by an infant concerned in the estate with the deceased person.

<!-- l4: decide:one person takes the whole of the property distributable under this Act -->

**83.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, one person takes the whole of the property distributable under this Act if—

    (a) count with the persons entitled to succeed beneficially, and their shares with the deceased person is equal to 1; and

    (b) the total of the shares distributed with the deceased person is equal to 1.

## Worked facts — the fixtures

<!-- l4: decide:an ISA person -->

**84.** In relation to a STRING “the name”, a Vital status “his vital status”, an optional DATE “his date of birth”, a BOOLEAN “conceived in the womb at the death”, a Money “the advancement” and a list of Child “his children”, an ISA person means Person where name is the name, the reference for this person is the name, date of birth is his date of birth, vital status is his vital status, children is his children, at the date of the death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive is conceived in the womb at the death, money or other property given, paid or settled by the intestate during his life to or for the advancement of the person is the advancement, the date on which the person attains the age of majority is NOTHING, a soldier being in actual military service is FALSE, a mariner or seaman being at sea is FALSE, a member of any naval or marine forces so circumstanced that if he were a soldier he would be in actual military service is FALSE, so desires that letters of administration be granted to such person as the court thinks fit is FALSE, lacks mental capacity (within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act 2008) to make decisions with respect to the management and administration of the person's property and affairs is FALSE, absent from Singapore is FALSE and willing to act is TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:living, childless -->

**85.** In relation to a STRING “the name”, living, childless means an ISA person with the name, living, NOTHING, FALSE, 0 and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:living, with children -->

**86.** In relation to a STRING “the name” and a list of Child “his children”, living, with children means an ISA person with the name, living, NOTHING, FALSE, 0 and his children.

<!-- l4: decide:who died on -->

**87.** In relation to a STRING “the name”, a DATE “the date of his death” and a list of Child “his children”, who died on means an ISA person with the name, died on with the date of his death, NOTHING, FALSE, 0 and his children.

<!-- l4: decide:an ISA legitimate child -->

**88.** In relation to a Person “the person”, an ISA legitimate child means Child where the child is the person, a legitimate child of the person whose child he is is TRUE and adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a child adopted by order of court in Singapore -->

**89.** In relation to a Person “the person”, a child adopted by order of court in Singapore means Child where the child is the person, a legitimate child of the person whose child he is is FALSE and adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam is TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:a child neither legitimate nor adopted -->

**90.** In relation to a Person “the person”, a child neither legitimate nor adopted means Child where the child is the person, a legitimate child of the person whose child he is is FALSE and adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a subsisting marriage to -->

**91.** In relation to a Person “the husband or wife”, a subsisting marriage to means Marriage where the spouse is the husband or wife, the date of the solemnisation of the marriage is NOTHING and subsisting at the death of the deceased, in the sense of not dissolved or annulled before the death is TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:of the whole blood, -->

**92.** In relation to a Person “the person”, of the whole blood, means Collateral relative where the relative is the person and of the whole blood or of the half blood is of the whole blood.

<!-- l4: decide:of the half blood, -->

**93.** In relation to a Person “the person”, of the half blood, means Collateral relative where the relative is the person and of the whole blood or of the half blood is of the half blood.

<!-- l4: decide:an ISA family -->

**94.** In relation to a list of Marriage “the marriages”, an optional Person “the father”, an optional Person “the mother”, a list of Collateral relative “the brothers and sisters”, a list of Person “the grandparents” and a list of Collateral relative “the uncles and aunts”, an ISA family means Family where the marriages of the deceased is the marriages, the father of the deceased is the father, the mother of the deceased is the mother, the brothers and sisters of the deceased is the brothers and sisters, the grandparents of the deceased is the grandparents and the uncles and aunts of the deceased is the uncles and aunts.

<!-- l4: decide:no family in evidence -->

**95.** No family in evidence means an ISA family with EMPTY, NOTHING, NOTHING, EMPTY, EMPTY and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:an ISA estate -->

**96.** In relation to a Money “movable in Singapore”, a Money “immovable in Singapore”, a Money “movable outside Singapore”, a Money “immovable outside Singapore”, a Money “the expenses of due administration”, a Money “the value disposed of by the will”, a Money “held as trustee and not beneficially, in Singapore” and a Money “the debts and liabilities”, an ISA estate means Estate where the value of the movable property situated in Singapore is movable in Singapore, the value of the immovable property situated in Singapore is immovable in Singapore, the value of the movable property situated outside Singapore is movable outside Singapore, the value of the immovable property situated outside Singapore is immovable outside Singapore, the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore is held as trustee and not beneficially, in Singapore, the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated outside Singapore is 0, the value of any moneys payable by an appointed insurer pursuant to the Dependants’ Protection Insurance Scheme or any other equivalent scheme maintained by the Central Provident Fund Board is 0, the value of the property administered by the Public Trustee is 0, the amount of the funds in court directed to be paid, transferred or delivered to him is 0, the value of land settled previously to the death of the deceased is 0, the trustees of the settlement is EMPTY, the value of the interest in property which at the time of his death is charged with the payment of money is 0, the amount of the charge on that interest is 0, the deceased has by will, deed or other document signified a contrary or other intention is FALSE, the debts and liabilities of the deceased is the debts and liabilities, the funeral, testamentary and administration expenses is the expenses of due administration, the creditors of the deceased is EMPTY, fully administered is FALSE and the value of the property beneficially disposed of by the will is the value disposed of by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:a beneficial gift -->

**97.** In relation to a Person “the taker”, a Kind of disposition “the kind” and a Money “the value”, a beneficial gift means Disposition where the donee is an individual with the taker, the kind of disposition is the kind, the value of the disposition is the value, beneficial is TRUE and not determinable at or before the death of the donee is TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:a disposition that is not beneficial -->

**98.** In relation to a Person “the taker”, a Kind of disposition “the kind” and a Money “the value”, a disposition that is not beneficial means Disposition where the donee is an individual with the taker, the kind of disposition is the kind, the value of the disposition is the value, beneficial is FALSE and not determinable at or before the death of the donee is TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:a duly executed will -->

**99.** In relation to a Person “the maker of the will”, a list of Disposition “the dispositions” and a BOOLEAN “the personal representative may take the undisposed part beneficially”, a duly executed will means Will where the testator is the maker of the will, the date of execution is NOTHING, in writing is TRUE, signed at the foot or end thereof by the testator is TRUE, signed at the foot or end thereof by some other person in his presence and by his direction is FALSE, the signature made or acknowledged by the testator as the signature to his will or codicil in the presence of 2 or more witnesses present at the same time is TRUE, apparent on the face of the will that the testator intended to give effect by such his signature to the writing signed as his will is TRUE, the attesting witnesses is EMPTY, the executors appointed by the will is EMPTY, the guardians of infant children appointed by the will is EMPTY, the dispositions made by the will is the dispositions, expressed to be made in contemplation of a marriage is FALSE, the reference for the person with whom the marriage contemplated was to be solemnised is NOTHING, made in exercise of a power of appointment is FALSE, the estate thereby appointed would not in default of such appointment pass to his or her heir, executor or administrator or the person entitled under the Intestate Succession Act 1967 is FALSE, the life interests arising under the will is EMPTY, it appears by the will that the personal representative is entitled to take that part beneficially is the personal representative may take the undisposed part beneficially and the codicils is EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:an ISA deceased person, with infants concerned in the estate -->

**100.** In relation to a Person “the intestate”, a Family “his family”, an Estate “his estate”, an optional Will “his will”, a BOOLEAN “domiciled in Singapore”, a BOOLEAN “he was a Muslim” and a list of Infant “the infants concerned in the estate”, an ISA deceased person, with infants concerned in the estate means Deceased person where the deceased is the intestate, the family is his family, the estate is his estate, the will is his will, domiciled in Singapore at the time of his death is domiciled in Singapore, carried on business or resided in Singapore within 12 months of his death is TRUE, a Muslim is he was a Muslim, the grants made in respect of the estate is EMPTY, the probate applications made in respect of the estate is EMPTY, a next of kin, creditor or other person has appeared and made out a claim to letters of administration is FALSE and the infants concerned in the estate is the infants concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:an ISA deceased person -->

**101.** In relation to a Person “the intestate”, a Family “his family”, an Estate “his estate”, an optional Will “his will”, a BOOLEAN “domiciled in Singapore” and a BOOLEAN “he was a Muslim”, an ISA deceased person means an ISA deceased person, with infants concerned in the estate with the intestate, his family, his estate, his will, domiciled in Singapore, he was a Muslim and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:an ISA guardian of the property of the infant -->

**102.** In relation to a Person “the person”, a STRING “the reference for the infant he is guardian of”, a How the guardian was appointed “how he was appointed” and an Alone or jointly “alone, or jointly with”, an ISA guardian of the property of the infant means Guardian where the guardian is the person, the reference for the infant is the reference for the infant he is guardian of, how the guardian was appointed is how he was appointed, of the person or of the property is guardian of the property of the infant, alone or jointly is alone, or jointly with, refuses to act is FALSE, the mother or father objects to his so acting is FALSE, considers that the mother or father is unfit to have the custody of the infant is FALSE, removed from his guardianship by the court is FALSE, has given security is TRUE, the court has otherwise ordered as to security is FALSE, has sold, mortgaged, exchanged, or otherwise parted with the possession of any of the movable or immovable property of the infant is FALSE, has leased land belonging to the infant is FALSE, the term of the lease, in years is NOTHING, has the permission of the court to deal with the property of the infant is FALSE, has given a good discharge for a legacy or other capital moneys payable to or receivable by the infant is TRUE, the court has otherwise ordered as to giving a good discharge is FALSE, the provision made out of the income of the property of the infant for his maintenance and education is A periodical sum where the sum is 0 and the period is monthly and has the permission of the court to apply a sum exceeding $100 per month is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an ISA infant concerned in the estate -->

**103.** In relation to a Person “the child”, an optional Person “his father”, an optional Person “his mother”, a list of Guardian “his guardians” and a Money “the capital of his property”, an ISA infant concerned in the estate means Infant where the infant is the child, the father of the infant is his father, the mother of the infant is his mother, the guardians of the infant is his guardians, some other person has parental rights with respect to him is FALSE, the income of the property of the infant is 0, the capital of the property of the infant is the capital of his property and of an age to express an independent opinion is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a Singapore estate of one million after expenses -->

**104.** A Singapore estate of one million after expenses means an ISA estate with 900000, 300000, 0, 0, 200000, 0, 0 and 0.

